## Observed

A torus rank (`FABRIC_2D_TORUS_*`) compiles Z routers with DA/FLA on. A mesh rank (`FABRIC_2D`) compiles the other end of the same Z cable with DA/FLA off. Payload still flows; the torus sender waits for ACKs the mesh receiver never sends, so the Z pair starves.

`need_deadlock_avoidance_support()` only checks N/S and E/W, so Z falls through and returns true under torus:

```cpp
// tt_metal/fabric/fabric_context.cpp
bool FabricContext::need_deadlock_avoidance_support(eth_chan_directions direction) const {
    if (topology_ == Topology::Ring) {
        return true;
    }
    if (topology_ == Topology::Torus) {
        const auto fabric_type = get_fabric_type(fabric_config_, is_ubb_galaxy_);
        const bool is_north_south =
            (direction == eth_chan_directions::NORTH || direction == eth_chan_directions::SOUTH);
        const bool is_east_west =
            (direction == eth_chan_directions::EAST || direction == eth_chan_directions::WEST);

        const bool torus_mismatch = (fabric_type == FabricType::TORUS_X && is_north_south) ||
                                    (fabric_type == FabricType::TORUS_Y && is_east_west);

        return !torus_mismatch;
    }
    return false;
}
```

## Expected

`need_deadlock_avoidance_support(Z)` must be false under torus. Both ends of a Z cable must use the same DA/FLA polarity.

```cpp
const bool is_z = (direction == eth_chan_directions::Z);
const bool torus_mismatch = (fabric_type == FabricType::TORUS_X && is_north_south) ||
                            (fabric_type == FabricType::TORUS_Y && is_east_west) ||
                            is_z;
```

## Steps to Reproduce

1. Multi-mesh Blackhole MGD with a Z intermesh cable (e.g. M2↔M3 ch4/ch5).
2. One rank `FABRIC_2D_TORUS_Y`, peer rank `FABRIC_2D`.
3. Traffic across that Z pair hangs on credit return.
